# List of patterns used to exclude file from beeing scanned in fossid.
# Files matching any of the patterns will not be transferred to fossid.
#
# Patterns are interpreted with groovy (java) regular expressions using find()
#
# Remarks:
# Input is a list of files determined by the git command git ls-files
# git ls-files uses "/" as directory separator. 
#
# Lines starting with # will be treated as comment
#
# Regex: The chars "[]().\^$|?*+{}" must be escaped with "\". IMPORTANT: "." needs to be replaced by "\."
# ^ matches the start of the string, 
# $ matches the end of the string
# (^|/) Start of filename or foldername: in root or as part of a folder
#
# See also: https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/util/regex/Pattern.html
# All the patterns are matched CASE INSENSITIVE
#
# all these root folders contains tests which are not delivered

(^|/)private/src/test/